---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

// Unlisted: no nav link. Reads as a straight root cause analysis until the
// last section, where the one component that was never eliminated is named.

const eliminated = [
  ['Hardware', 'Swapped for an identical unit, then for a different vendor’s unit', ],
  ['Operating system', 'Reimaged. Reproduced on Windows 11, macOS and Ubuntu', ],
  ['Network', 'Wired, Wi-Fi, tethered 5G, fully offline', ],
  ['Application', 'Repaired, reinstalled, rolled back three versions, replaced with a competitor', ],
  ['User profile', 'New profile, new account, new tenant', ],
  ['Peripherals', 'Keyboard, mouse and display replaced', ],
  ['Power', 'Different socket, UPS, different building', ],
  ['Time', 'Reproduced across time zones, a DST change and a leap second', ],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Error ID-10-T"
  image="/images/og-card-id-10-t.png"
  description="A root cause analysis of error ID-10-T: symptoms, affected configurations, reproduction, elimination and the root cause."
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <div class="container rca">
      <article>
        <header class="article-header">
          <h1>Error ID-10-T: a root cause analysis</h1>
          <div class="post-meta">
            <span>Scott McAllister</span>
            <time datetime="2026-09-22">22 Sep 2026</time>
            <span>Severity: persistent</span>
            <span class="rca-state"><span class="led" style="--led-period:1.2s"></span>Root cause identified</span>
          </div>
        </header>

        <div class="prose">
          <p class="rca-lede">
            ID-10-T is the most frequently reported fault in end-user computing and the least frequently fixed.
            It has been seen on every platform, every release and every configuration that shipped with a person attached.
            It survives reimaging, hardware replacement and change of vendor. It has no knowledge-base article, no hotfix and no owner.
            This document traces it to its source.
          </p>

          <h2 id="symptoms">Symptoms</h2>
          <p>
            Reports arrive with high urgency and low detail. The reported symptom and the observed state of the system rarely agree,
            and the fault is usually gone by the time an engineer attaches to the session.
          </p>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>As reported</th><th>As observed</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>“The internet is down.”</td><td>One browser tab failing to load. Every other service healthy.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>“My password stopped working.”</td><td>Fourteen failed sign-ins in four minutes, followed by a lockout. Caps Lock on.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>“The screen is completely dead.”</td><td>Device powered and responsive. Display off at its own switch.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>“I haven’t changed anything.”</td><td>Eleven configuration changes in the preceding hour, each made interactively.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>“It just started working again.”</td><td>No system-side change logged between failure and recovery.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>
            That last row matters most. In a normal incident, recovery follows a change: a patch, a restart, a failover.
            With ID-10-T, the system logs nothing between broken and fixed. Whatever changed isn’t visible to the system.
          </p>

          <h2 id="affected">Affected configurations</h2>
          <p>All of them. Including, as far as this page can tell, yours:</p>
          <dl class="rca-config" data-config>
            <div><dt>Platform</dt><dd data-c="os">Not detected</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Browser</dt><dd data-c="browser">Not detected</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Viewport</dt><dd data-c="viewport">Not detected</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Local time</dt><dd data-c="time">Not detected</dd></div>
            <div class="rca-config-verdict"><dt>Status</dt><dd>Affected</dd></div>
          </dl>

          <h2 id="identifier">The identifier</h2>
          <p>
            The code doesn’t fit any error-code scheme in use. It isn’t an HRESULT, which would read <code>0x8007xxxx</code> or similar.
            It isn’t an NTSTATUS, a Win32 system error, an <code>errno</code> value or an HTTP status.
            It returns nothing from Microsoft’s Error Lookup tool.
            It isn’t among the 597 ConfigMgr and Intune codes in the list behind
            <a href="/projects/search-json-for-error-codes">Search-JsonForErrorCodes</a>. I checked.
          </p>
          <p>
            No vendor has registered it, yet support staff everywhere use it and recognise it immediately.
            It spreads by word of mouth, mostly among helpdesk staff and mostly out of the user’s hearing.
            That’s unusual for an error code, and it’s the first sign that this one doesn’t describe the system.
          </p>

          <h2 id="reproduction">Reproduction</h2>
          <p>A representative session, taken from a support trace:</p>
          <pre class="rca-trace"><code><span class="t">09:14:02.118</span> <span class="i">INFO</span>  session.start      device=healthy  network=healthy
<span class="t">09:14:02.301</span> <span class="i">INFO</span>  ticket.open        priority=URGENT  subject="nothing works"
<span class="t">09:14:40.552</span> <span class="i">INFO</span>  engineer.attach    remote=true
<span class="t">09:14:41.007</span> <span class="i">INFO</span>  diag.run           cpu=ok  mem=ok  disk=ok  net=ok  app=ok
<span class="t">09:15:30.920</span> <span class="w">WARN</span>  diag.result        fault=not_reproduced
<span class="t">09:16:12.334</span> <span class="i">INFO</span>  engineer.detach
<span class="t">09:16:58.781</span> <span class="e">ERROR</span> fault.recur        code=ID-10-T  device=healthy  network=healthy
<span class="t">09:17:03.114</span> <span class="i">INFO</span>  engineer.attach    remote=true
<span class="t">09:17:03.900</span> <span class="w">WARN</span>  diag.result        fault=not_reproduced
<span class="t">09:18:44.265</span> <span class="i">INFO</span>  ticket.resolve     resolution="started working on its own"</code></pre>
          <p>
            Two observations. The fault never reproduces while an engineer is watching, and it comes back within a minute of them leaving.
            Faults that go quiet under observation usually point at the observer. Here they point at whoever was left in the session when the observer went.
          </p>

          <h2 id="elimination">Elimination</h2>
          <p>
            The standard method: change one component at a time and see whether the fault survives.
            A component whose replacement leaves the fault in place is not the cause.
          </p>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table class="rca-matrix">
              <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Method</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                {eliminated.map(([c, m]) => (
                  <tr>
                    <td class="rca-comp">{c}</td>
                    <td>{m}</td>
                    <td class="rca-out">Eliminated</td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
                <tr class="rca-remaining">
                  <td class="rca-comp"><span class="rca-redact" aria-label="Withheld">withheld</span></td>
                  <td>Could not be replaced. Fault present in 100% of sessions, on every configuration, at every site.</td>
                  <td class="rca-out">Not eliminated</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>
            Eight components replaced, eight eliminated. One component remained in every reproduction and could not be swapped out for testing.
            That makes it the only candidate left.
          </p>

          <h2 id="cause">Root cause</h2>
          <p>
            The fault is not in the system under test. Every layer of that system has been replaced and the fault carried on regardless.
            It sits at the interface between the system and whoever is using it, on the far side of that interface, where logging doesn’t reach.
          </p>
          <p>
            That fits every finding above. It explains why the fault follows the user across devices, why it disappears when a competent observer attaches,
            why no configuration change appears between failure and recovery, and why no vendor will put its name to the code.
          </p>
          <p>
            One step remains: decoding the identifier itself. Read it as characters rather than as a code, and substitute each numeral with the letter it most resembles.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <section class="rca-reveal" aria-labelledby="reveal-heading" data-reveal>
        <p class="rca-decode" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>I</span><span>D</span><span class="rca-dash">-</span><span class="rca-flip" data-to="I">1</span><span class="rca-flip" data-to="O">0</span><span class="rca-dash">-</span><span>T</span>
        </p>
        <h2 id="reveal-heading" class="rca-hi">
          Hi.<br />
          It’s you.<br />
          <span class="rca-you">You’re the <span class="rca-nowrap">ID-10-T.</span></span>
        </h2>
        <dl class="rca-close">
          <div><dt>Component</dt><dd>You</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Resolution</dt><dd>Closed, won’t fix. Working as designed.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Time spent reading about yourself</dt><dd data-dwell>Not measured</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="emote-panel">
          <img
            src="/images/emotes/self.png"
            alt="Pixel-art illustration of Scott holding a tiny version of himself overhead next to a recycling bin"
            width="60"
            height="60"
          />
          <span class="emote-caption">Archiving: operator.exe</span>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  const ua = navigator.userAgent;
  const os =
    /iPhone|iPad/.test(ua) ? 'iOS' :
    /Android/.test(ua) ? 'Android' :
    /Mac OS X/.test(ua) ? 'macOS' :
    /Windows/.test(ua) ? 'Windows' :
    /CrOS/.test(ua) ? 'ChromeOS' :
    /Linux/.test(ua) ? 'Linux' : '';
  const browser =
    /Edg\//.test(ua) ? 'Edge' :
    /Firefox\//.test(ua) ? 'Firefox' :
    /Chrome\//.test(ua) ? 'Chrome' :
    /Safari\//.test(ua) ? 'Safari' : '';
  const set = (k: string, v: string) => {
    const el = document.querySelector(`[data-c="${k}"]`);
    if (el && v) el.textContent = v;
  };
  set('os', os);
  set('browser', browser);
  if (innerWidth) set('viewport', `${innerWidth} × ${innerHeight}`);
  set('time', new Date().toLocaleTimeString([], { hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit' }));

  // The decode plays once, when the reveal is reached. Reduced motion gets
  // the decoded letters straight away.
  const reveal = document.querySelector('[data-reveal]') as HTMLElement;
  const dwell = reveal.querySelector('[data-dwell]') as HTMLElement;
  const start = performance.now();
  new IntersectionObserver((entries, obs) => {
    if (!entries[0].isIntersecting) return;
    obs.disconnect();
    const s = Math.round((performance.now() - start) / 1000);
    dwell.textContent = s < 60 ? `${s} second${s === 1 ? '' : 's'}` : `${Math.floor(s / 60)} min ${s % 60} s`;
    reveal.classList.add('is-decoded');
    reveal.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.rca-flip').forEach((el) => {
      setTimeout(() => (el.textContent = el.dataset.to!), matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches ? 0 : 450);
    });
  }, { threshold: 0.4 }).observe(reveal);
</script>

<style>
  .rca-state {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    color: var(--green);
  }
  .rca-lede {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .rca-config {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(9.5rem, 1fr));
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--panel);
  }
  .rca-config div {
    padding: 0.8rem 1.1rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .rca-config div:last-child {
    border-right: 0;
  }
  .rca-config dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .rca-config dd {
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .rca-config-verdict dd {
    color: var(--red);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .rca-trace {
    background: var(--panel);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    white-space: pre;
  }
  .rca-trace .t { color: var(--dim); }
  .rca-trace .i { color: var(--cyan); }
  .rca-trace .w { color: var(--amber); }
  .rca-trace .e { color: var(--red); font-weight: 700; }
  .rca-matrix .rca-comp {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .rca-matrix .rca-out {
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .rca-matrix tbody tr:not(.rca-remaining) .rca-comp {
    text-decoration: line-through;
    text-decoration-color: var(--dim);
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .rca-remaining td {
    background: var(--panel-2);
  }
  .rca-remaining .rca-out {
    color: var(--red);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .rca-redact {
    display: inline-block;
    min-width: 5.5em;
    background: var(--text);
    color: transparent;
    border-radius: 2px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    user-select: none;
  }

  /* The reveal. Everything above is the report; this is the finding. */
  .rca-reveal {
    margin: 6rem 0 3rem;
    padding-top: 3rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .rca-decode {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.35em;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 4vw, 2rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .rca-decode span {
    display: inline-block;
    min-width: 0.7em;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .rca-flip {
    transition: color 600ms cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }
  .is-decoded .rca-flip {
    color: var(--amber);
  }
  .is-decoded .rca-dash {
    opacity: 0.3;
  }
  .rca-hi {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 5.4rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
    color: var(--text);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .rca-you {
    color: var(--amber);
  }
  .rca-nowrap {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .rca-close {
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    max-width: 34rem;
  }
  .rca-close div {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.55rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .rca-close dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .rca-close dd {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: right;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .rca-config div {
      border-right: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .rca-config div:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }
    .rca-close div {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.1rem;
    }
    .rca-close dd {
      text-align: left;
    }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .rca-flip { transition: none; }
  }
</style>
